{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_architecture_design_principles", "label": "Non-negotiable design principles", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a70", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stated as absolute so convenience cannot win an argument: a change violating one is wrong regardless of how convenient it is."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_agent_never_holds_key", "label": "Principle 1 \u2014 the agent never holds a private key", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a70.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Autonomous code only writes proposals to a queue; only a human-triggered process gated by Ledger hardware confirmation can move funds."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_no_pii_on_chain", "label": "Principle 2 \u2014 no raw PII on-chain, commitment hashes only", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a70.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "On-chain data is permanent and public and encryption does not fix that, so only fixed-size commitment hashes go on-chain and raw data stays off-chain, encrypted."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_evidence_record_per_action", "label": "Principle 3 \u2014 every state change produces an evidence record", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a70.3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An action is not complete until its record is appended to the hash chain, so the audit trail cannot lag behind reality."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_confidential_vendor_matching", "label": "Principle 4 \u2014 confidential vendor matching runs in a TEE", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a70.4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Checks against vendor PII run inside the Chainlink CRE TEE handler rather than the main API process; a non-confidential fallback behind the same interface means the rest of the system does not care which is active."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_signing_readonly_process_split", "label": "Principle 5 \u2014 signing and read-only are separate processes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a70.5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Architectural separation, not just separate code paths, so a bug in the read path cannot reach a key."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_system_architecture", "label": "System architecture (web / api / bridge / CRE / contracts / Hedera)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "approval-bridge runs on the approver's local machine because it is the only process with USB access to the Ledger; apps/api never talks to the device directly."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_monorepo_structure", "label": "Monorepo structure (pnpm workspaces, TypeScript everywhere)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every external SDK in scope is npm/TS-native, so there is no reason to introduce a second language anywhere in the stack."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_vendor", "label": "Vendor model", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "digilockerUserId is the identity primary key, never the Aadhaar number: receiving a full Aadhaar number would create Data Vault obligations this flow otherwise avoids."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_vendorwallet", "label": "VendorWallet model", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "controlProofSig proves wallet custody only, never that the signer represents the named legal entity, so it is never alone sufficient for CONFIRMED."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_paymentrequest", "label": "PaymentRequest model", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_approvalevent", "label": "ApprovalEvent model", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "selfieCheckProofRef holds an opaque reference to the stored IDKit result, not the raw proof."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_recipientacknowledgment", "label": "RecipientAcknowledgment model", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_exceptioncase", "label": "ExceptionCase model", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_evidencerecord", "label": "EvidenceRecord model", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_verificationtier", "label": "VerificationTier (TIER0-TIER3)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tier gates the decision engine: a high-value payment to a liveness-only payee must return REVERIFY, and thresholds live in config because different customers set different risk appetites."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_paymentdecision", "label": "PaymentDecision (SAFE_TO_SEND / DO_NOT_SEND / REVERIFY / SEND_TEST_AMOUNT)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_decide", "label": "decide() decision engine state machine", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Written as one explicit pure function rather than scattered if/else so every branch is auditable and testable by direct input injection; hard blocks are ordered before soft ones and first match wins."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_tier_thresholds", "label": "TierThresholds config", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_identityprovider", "label": "IdentityProvider interface", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pluggable so non-India payees fall through to a generic provider \u2014 the same pattern as VendorMatcher."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_digilockerprovider", "label": "DigiLockerProvider (India, Sandbox aggregator)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The human consent step cannot be automated, and that is the point \u2014 it is what makes DigiLocker legally defensible as an identity source. One consent flow satisfies legal identity + address + photo + tax ID at once, reaching TIER3_ADDRESS in a single step, so the postcard path is unnecessary for India."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_mockidentityprovider", "label": "MockIdentityProvider (fixture replay)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.7.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Live KYC calls are billed per request, so development replays a recorded capture. Mock mode must still walk created -> succeeded via a local stub page rather than short-circuiting, or bugs in the polling path go uncaught."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_generickycprovider", "label": "GenericKycProvider (Persona/Onfido/Sumsub)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_vendormatcher", "label": "VendorMatcher interface", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The decision engine is wired against the interface, not a concrete class, so swapping fallback for CRE is a one-line dependency-injection change."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_fallbackvendormatcher", "label": "FallbackVendorMatcher (non-confidential)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Built and wired first because it is what makes the whole pipeline demoable without waiting on CRE enrollment."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_cre_vendor_match_workflow", "label": "CRE TEE vendor-match workflow (cre.handlerInTee)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ConfidentialHTTPClient is deliberately not used \u2014 it lacks the TeeRuntime overload a TEE handler requires. Only the verdict crosses the enclave boundary, and the simulator is treated as logic verification only, never as a security demonstration."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_onboardingsessionnonce", "label": "onboardingSessionNonce session binding", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each check can individually pass while belonging to different people \u2014 an attacker can pair a borrowed genuine KYC session with their own wallet signature. An identical nonce across the liveness check, the document check and the wallet-control signature chains legal identity -> live face -> wallet key into one subject instead of three independent facts."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_identity_binding", "label": "Identity-to-wallet binding (EIP-712 IdentityBinding)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "DigiLocker proves who someone is and EIP-712 proves what key they hold; neither alone maps identity to a wallet. The signed attestation turns a data-entry claim into a repudiation-resistant act by the payee, usable in recovery proceedings."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_business_payee_spoofing_control", "label": "registryVerifiedContact independent-channel callback control", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An attacker submitting a real company's name and tax ID with their own wallet and phone would confirm their own fraud if the callback dialled the submitted number, so the contact comes only from an independent registry lookup or a contact on file predating the change \u2014 never the current submission. Seed data hardcodes one so the real control logic still executes in demos."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_xmldsig_verification", "label": "Check 1 \u2014 XMLDSig signature verification", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Parsing the XML without verifying the signature throws away the entire security property \u2014 an unverified XML is just a text file."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_cross_document_consistency", "label": "Check 2 \u2014 cross-document consistency", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Name, dob and gender disagreement between Aadhaar and PAN is a strong fraud signal and must block CONFIRMED."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_same_subject_linkage", "label": "Check 3 \u2014 same-subject linkage", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The DigiLocker user id appears in both the PAN Person uid and the Aadhaar KycRes txn string; asserting equality is what proves the two documents describe one person."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_ttl_enforcement", "label": "Check 4 \u2014 KYC TTL enforcement", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CONFIRMED is time-bounded, not permanent: the observed KycRes ttl is issue + 1 year, so re-verification is scheduled before expiry."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_normalisation_layer", "label": "Mandatory format normalisation before comparison", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.7.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The same person's details come back formatted three different ways across endpoints (19/11/2001 vs 19-11-2001; male/M/MALE; mixed-case names), so naive equality rejects a legitimate user \u2014 the single most likely bug in the integration. The profile date_of_birth is documented as unix-ms but returned DD/MM/YYYY live, so both types must be handled."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_fixture_tiers", "label": "Two fixture tiers (real gitignored, synthetic committed)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.7.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Redaction is impossible: editing one byte of the signed XML invalidates the XMLDSig signature, so there is no redacted-but-valid variant. index.json doubles as the test oracle and is read at runtime rather than hardcoded, because the expected values identify a real person."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_evidence_hash_chain", "label": "Evidence hash chain", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.8", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every state-changing write inserts a record in the same transaction, linked to its predecessor's hash, so insertion, removal or edit is detectable on read."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_canonicalize", "label": "canonicalize() deterministic JSON", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.8", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "JSON.stringify preserves insertion order, which is not guaranteed across engines and versions, so two equal payloads built differently would hash differently."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_computerecordhash", "label": "computeRecordHash()", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.8", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_hcs_anchoring", "label": "Batch HCS Merkle anchoring job", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.8", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_hedera_ats", "label": "Hedera ATS receivable tokenization", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Control List, Pause and Lock modules are configured on deploy; the receivable is tokenized as a bond-like instrument only after the vendor is CONFIRMED and the decision permits sending."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_identity_registry_hook", "label": "GET /internal/identity-registry/:address hook", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The real integration point: it makes the platform's own KYC data the compliance backend that ATS's ERC-3643 mode calls out to, rather than a cosmetic add-on."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_world_id_selfie_check", "label": "World ID Selfie Check (approver second factor)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.6", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Proves a real distinct human independently of the specific hardware key holder that Clear Signing proves. Medium assurance only, so UI copy must say 'a live human confirmed this action', never 'identity verified'."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_approval_bridge", "label": "apps/approval-bridge", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Runs on the approver's local machine, never cloud infra, because it is the only process with USB access to the Ledger. The device transport is an env var so the code path stays identical for USB and Speculos."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_clear_signing", "label": "Ledger Clear Signing on-device confirmation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The confirm/reject happens on the physical device screen and the CLI call blocks until the device responds, so the recipient and amount a human sees are the ones actually signed."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_auth_role_separation", "label": "agent / approver role separation at the API layer", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The literal implementation of principle 1: separate keys per role enforced in middleware rather than the UI, with a test asserting an agent-scoped token is refused on /approvals/*."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_architecture_system_architecture", "target": "docs_architecture_design_principles", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_approval_bridge", "target": "docs_architecture_agent_never_holds_key", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_approval_bridge", "target": "docs_architecture_clear_signing", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_auth_role_separation", "target": "docs_architecture_agent_never_holds_key", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_evidence_hash_chain", "target": "docs_architecture_evidence_record_per_action", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_cre_vendor_match_workflow", "target": "docs_architecture_confidential_vendor_matching", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_cre_vendor_match_workflow", "target": "docs_architecture_vendormatcher", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_fallbackvendormatcher", "target": "docs_architecture_vendormatcher", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_digilockerprovider", "target": "docs_architecture_identityprovider", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_mockidentityprovide